Z||000011||Formula88||12-24-2001||09:43 AM||||Good car.  I'm also a PC Tech driving a Grand Am!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I was originally looking for a mid-90's Sunbird, etc., but with my credit, I couldn't get the loan.  But, wait, they WILL loan me money on a used '99 program car! (this was in March, 99).  So I ended up getting a 99 Grand Am with 24K miles on it back in March 99.  Awesome car, I do like it, but way more car payment than I wanted.  That and I'm killing it's value - it's currently got over 70K miles.  Yup, I drive alot too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Is yours a 5-speed or automatic?<BR>You might check out <A HREF="http://www.grandamgt.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.grandamgt.com</A>  .  It's primarily for 99+ Grand Am GT's, but they're also friendly to all Grand Ams.  It's a good site for info on parts, etc.  Their's also <A HREF="http://www.n-body.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.n-body.net</A>  for all N-Body cars (Grand Am included).<P>Have fun with the new car.  It's not a Fiero, but a good one nevertheless. ||||reg||14
Z||000012||8Ball||12-24-2001||04:54 PM||||Mine is the 4 speed auto with overdrive. I am already a member at grandamgt.com   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I am 8Ball there as well I will check out the other site as well. I just love this little car. Like you said it is not a Fiero but it is still fun to drive   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And it will throw me back in the seat when i punch it as well   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Gotta love that   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 8Ball (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
